DiveSaveEd — Dave The Diver Save Editor for macOS
Attribution & Notices
==================================================

This project is an independent, native macOS save editor for the game
"Dave the Diver". The Swift application code is an independent
reimplementation. The bundled reference data is not.

Derived work — DaveSaveEd (MIT)
-------------------------------
The bundled item/ingredient reference database
(Sources/DaveSaveCore/Resources/reference.sqlite) is generated by inflating the
embedded SQL blob from FNGarvin/DaveSaveEd (embedded_sql.h) and is therefore a
derivative of that MIT-licensed work. The inflated output is byte-identical to
reference.sql in this repository. Its MIT notice is reproduced in full in
THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md, as MIT requires.

  https://github.com/FNGarvin/DaveSaveEd — by FNGarvin, MIT.

The database is regenerable, not hand-curated: see Scripts/gen_refdb.sh and
Scripts/inflate_embedded_sql.py. It contains 563 item rows and 305 ingredient
rows consisting solely of internal identifier keys (text, description and asset
reference keys such as "Bacon_Relic" and "Drone_Chip") and numeric balance
parameters (ItemWeight, ItemBuyPrice, ItemSellPrice, ItemMaxStackCount,
MaxCount, DLCType and similar). It contains no localized display text, no item
descriptions, no icon or sprite data, and no dialogue.

The macOS and Windows save-path knowledge, and the shape of the feature set
(max Gold / Bei / Artisan's Flame / Follower count / ingredients), are also
derived from or inspired by that project. Thank you.

Credit — save-format reverse-engineering
----------------------------------------
The correct char-level (UTF-16 code unit) XOR codec understanding — which lets
this editor handle non-ASCII (Chinese/Korean/Japanese) saves without corruption,
unlike byte-level implementations — was informed by
WhiteMinds/dave-diver-expansion (tools/save-codec, PORTING-NOTES). That
repository publishes no LICENSE file, so no license is asserted on its behalf;
file-format facts and algorithms are not copyrightable. This credit is offered
as a courtesy. Thank you.

  https://github.com/WhiteMinds/dave-diver-expansion

